(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Surgical complications including integumentary damage and contamination-related infections) Tj
T*
(remain significant morbidity factors in patients undergoing open cardiac surgery. This) Tj
T*
(trial compared a novel automated positioning device with standard passive dressing) Tj
T*
(techniques in reducing these adverse events. Sixty cardiac surgery patients were) Tj
T*
(randomized to either the intervention arm \(receiving the positioning device\) or control) Tj
T*
(arm \(standard dressing protocol\). Primary evaluation focused on dermal injury development) Tj
T*
(and infection rates measured at postoperative intervals. Secondary assessment included) Tj
T*
(staff acceptability scores. The positioning device group demonstrated markedly lower rates) Tj
T*
(of skin breakdown \(2% versus 71%, p = 0.002, relative risk 3.18\) compared to controls.) Tj
T*
(Infection rates showed a trend favoring the device \(3% versus 18%\), though this did not) Tj
T*
(reach statistical significance. Staff surveys indicated high satisfaction with the device) Tj
T*
(approach \(mean 4.82/5.0\). Implementation of mechanical positioning strategies may) Tj
T*
(substantially reduce integumentary complications in cardiac surgical populations.) Tj
